import{_ as i,o as a,c as e,ao as t}from"./chunks/framework.Fmz77R0w.js";const c=JSON.parse('{"title":"Samplers","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"samplers.md","filePath":"samplers.md","lastUpdated":null}'),n={name:"samplers.md"};function h(l,s,p,r,k,d){return a(),e("div",null,[...s[0]||(s[0]=[t(`<h1 id="Samplers" tabindex="-1">Samplers <a class="header-anchor" href="#Samplers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Samplers {#Samplers}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>A sampler decides which hyperparameters each trial gets. BigHOPs.jl has two kinds:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Full-budget samplers</strong> evaluate every trial once, at full cost. They are given the number of trials up front: <code>Hyperoptimizer(objective, candidates; sampler=..., n=...)</code>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Successive-halving samplers</strong> start many trials on a small resource (epochs, samples, iterations) and give more only to the best ones. The number of trials comes from their schedule: <code>Hyperoptimizer(objective, candidates, sampler)</code>.</p></li></ul><p>Every sampler is seeded by default, so repeating a search proposes the same trials.</p><h2 id="Full-budget-samplers" tabindex="-1">Full-budget samplers <a class="header-anchor" href="#Full-budget-samplers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Full-budget samplers {#Full-budget-samplers}&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="RandomSampler" tabindex="-1">RandomSampler <a class="header-anchor" href="#RandomSampler" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;RandomSampler {#RandomSampler}&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">RandomSampler</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(rng</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">StableRNG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">))</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Draws each trial&#39;s hyperparameters independently at random. It is the simplest baseline, and also the default inner sampler of <code>Hyperband</code> and <code>ASHA</code>.</p><h3 id="LHSampler" tabindex="-1">LHSampler <a class="header-anchor" href="#LHSampler" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;LHSampler {#LHSampler}&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">LHSampler</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(; rng</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">StableRNG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">))</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Draws all <code>n</code> trials up front as a Latin hypercube, which spreads them evenly along every hyperparameter. It warns if <code>n</code> is too small to cover every combination of discrete values. Each <code>LHSampler()</code> can back only one <code>Hyperoptimizer</code>.</p><h3 id="SobolSampler" tabindex="-1">SobolSampler <a class="header-anchor" href="#SobolSampler" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;SobolSampler {#SobolSampler}&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">SobolSampler</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(; rng</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">StableRNG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">))</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Takes each trial as the next point of a Sobol sequence, shifted by one random offset, so successive trials spread over the space more evenly than independent random draws. Unlike <code>LHSampler</code>, it needs no fixed number of trials; after any power-of-2 number of trials, each hyperparameter&#39;s range is covered evenly.</p><h3 id="GPSampler" tabindex="-1">GPSampler <a class="header-anchor" href="#GPSampler" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;GPSampler {#GPSampler}&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">GPSampler</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(gp; next_point, noise, n_initial, initial</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">SobolSampler</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(), fit_hyperparams</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">nothing</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">          standardize</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">BigHOPs</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">zscore, strict_initialization</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">true</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, rng</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">StableRNG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">))</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Models the objective as a Gaussian process over the hyperparameters. The first <code>n_initial</code> trials come from <code>initial</code>; after that, the GP is conditioned on every completed trial, and <code>next_point</code> chooses each new trial from the posterior. <code>ThompsonSampling(n_candidates; jitter)</code> is the provided <code>next_point</code>: it draws the posterior at <code>n_candidates</code> Sobol points and returns the one where the draw is lowest.</p><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">using</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> AbstractGPs</span></span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">sampler </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> GPSampler</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">GP</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">Matern52Kernel</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">()); next_point</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">ThompsonSampling</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">512</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">; jitter</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1e-6</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">),</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">                    noise</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1e-6</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, n_initial</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">10</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">ho </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> Hyperoptimizer</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(objective, candidates; sampler, n</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">50</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">)</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>fit_hyperparams(X, y)</code> can refit the kernel&#39;s hyperparameters, and optionally the noise, before each conditioning. See the <a href="./api">API</a> for the remaining options.</p><h2 id="Successive-halving-samplers" tabindex="-1">Successive-halving samplers <a class="header-anchor" href="#Successive-halving-samplers" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Successive-halving samplers {#Successive-halving-samplers}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>These samplers need an objective with a resource knob: the objective receives the resource level as <code>p.r</code>, and a larger <code>p.r</code> should mean a more expensive but more accurate evaluation, such as more training epochs. They share one schedule:</p><ul><li><p><code>R</code> is the largest resource level, given to the trials that survive every round;</p></li><li><p><code>r_min</code> is the smallest resource level, where the most aggressive bracket starts;</p></li><li><p><code>η</code> is the factor between rounds: after each round, the best <code>1/η</code> of the trials continue with <code>η</code> times the resource;</p></li><li><p><code>iterations</code> repeats the whole schedule.</p></li></ul><p>A bracket starts some number of trials at one resource level and halves its way up to <code>R</code>, and the schedule runs several brackets, from aggressive (many trials, starting at <code>r_min</code>) to conservative (a few trials, all at <code>R</code>).</p><p>When a trial is promoted to a higher resource level, it does not have to start again from scratch: with a <code>Stateful</code> objective, <code>Hyperband</code>, <code>ASHA</code> and <code>BOHB</code> pass it the earlier trial&#39;s state, so training can continue where it stopped, while <code>DEHB</code> trains every trial from scratch. See <a href="/BigHOPs.jl/previews/PR102/general_functionalities#Stateful-objectives">Stateful objectives</a>.</p><h3 id="Hyperband" tabindex="-1">Hyperband <a class="header-anchor" href="#Hyperband" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Hyperband {#Hyperband}&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">Hyperband</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(; R, η</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">3</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, r_min</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, iterations</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, inner</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">RandomSampler</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">())</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Successive halving as in Li et al. (2018): a rung must finish before any of its trials are promoted. <code>inner</code> draws the starting configurations, at random by default. When every open bracket is waiting on results and the executor has spare capacity, the next bracket starts.</p><h3 id="ASHA" tabindex="-1">ASHA <a class="header-anchor" href="#ASHA" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;ASHA {#ASHA}&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">ASHA</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(; R, η</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">3</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, r_min</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, iterations</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, inner</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">RandomSampler</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">())</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Asynchronous <code>Hyperband</code> (Li et al., 2020), with the same schedule and arguments: a trial is promoted as soon as it is among the best <code>1/η</code> completed so far in its rung, instead of waiting for the rung to finish. This keeps workers busy under <code>Threaded</code> or <code>DistributedQueue</code> when trial durations vary.</p><h3 id="DEHB" tabindex="-1">DEHB <a class="header-anchor" href="#DEHB" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;DEHB {#DEHB}&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">DEHB</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(; R, η</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">3</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, r_min</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, iterations</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, F</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">0.5</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, crossover</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">0.5</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, rng</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">StableRNG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">))</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>Hyperband</code>&#39;s schedule with differential evolution in place of random draws (Awad et al., 2021). Each resource level keeps a subpopulation of configurations; new trials are mutated and crossed over from them, so later trials build on the ones that did well. <code>F</code> is the mutation factor and <code>crossover</code> the crossover probability. Every trial trains from scratch, so a <code>Stateful</code> objective never receives a <code>pre_artefact</code>.</p><h3 id="BOHB" tabindex="-1">BOHB <a class="header-anchor" href="#BOHB" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;BOHB {#BOHB}&quot;">​</a></h3><div class="language-julia vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">julia</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">BOHB</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(; R, η</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">3</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, r_min</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, iterations</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, ρ</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">/</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">3</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, q</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">0.15</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, N_s</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">64</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, N_min</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">nothing</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, b_w</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">3</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">     min_bandwidth</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1e-3</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">, rng</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">StableRNG</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">1</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">))</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>Hyperband</code>&#39;s schedule with the first rung of each bracket drawn from kernel density estimates (Falkner et al., 2018), while promotions are as in <code>Hyperband</code>. Once a resource level has enough completed trials, they are split into the best ones and the rest, a density is fitted to each, and the next configuration is the one among <code>N_s</code> candidates that is most likely under the good density relative to the bad one. A fraction <code>ρ</code> of draws stays uniformly random, so the search keeps exploring.</p><p>The model needs more completed trials as the number of hyperparameters <code>d</code> grows: by default <code>N_min = d + 1</code>, and both the good and the bad set need more than <code>d</code> trials, so a resource level gets a model only after about <code>2d + 2</code> trials there.</p>`,37)])])}const g=i(n,[["render",h]]);export{c as __pageData,g as default};
